+All four existing gates belong to each operation's conversion invocation. Use
+their current human, automatic or skip policies from settings. The job plan is
+reviewed through Gate One, not a new fifth gate. Each operation's Gate One report
+references that plan and identifies its operation scope. Approval evidence must
+identify the current operation and gate, so approval of one operation does not
+silently approve another. With every gate set to human, a thousand operations can
+require four thousand gate decisions; users control the human pauses through
+the existing settings. Automatic or skipped human approval never bypasses failed
+technical checks, missing dependencies or cycles. A pending or rejected gate
+pauses the current operation; the coordinator does not advance.
 
